        "body": "I reproduced this with the jobparser itself, outside Forgejo. A small Go program calls `jobparser.Parse` on `a.yml` with `ExpandLocalReusableWorkflows`, using the three files above, and prints each resulting job's workflow-level env (`SingleWorkflow.Env`).\r\n\r\nThe result is the same on v12.10.2 (what Forgejo 15.0.11 vendors), on v12.13.2, and on main (v13.2.2-0.20261110144235-80c990d7b734):\r\n\r\n| Case | env of C's job `show` | Expected |\r\n| --- | --- | --- |\r\n| a → b → c (this issue) | `B_LEVEL=b` | `C_LEVEL=c` |\r\n| a → c (single level, fixed by #1499) | `C_LEVEL=c` | `C_LEVEL=c` |\r\n| a → b → c, with no `env:` in b | (empty) | `C_LEVEL=c` |\r\n\r\nSo at any nesting depth of two or more, C's own workflow-level env is dropped, even when the middle workflow declares no env at all. It is replaced by the middle workflow's env, which may be empty.\r\n\r\n`workflowLevelEnableOpenIDConnect` is reassigned the same way in `expandReusableWorkflow`, so a nested `enable-openid-connect` is probably affected too. I have not tested that.\r\n\r\nThe program, in case it helps for a test (it takes one directory per case, each holding `.forgejo/workflows/a.yml` and the workflows it calls):\r\n\r\n    package main\r\n\r\n    import (\r\n    \t\"fmt\"\r\n    \t\"os\"\r\n    \t\"path/filepath\"\r\n    \t\"sort\"\r\n    \t\"strings\"\r\n\r\n    \t\"code.forgejo.org/forgejo/runner/v12/act/jobparser\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    func main() {\r\n    \tfor _, root := range os.Args[1:] {\r\n    \t\tfetch := func(_ *jobparser.Job, path string) ([]byte, error) {\r\n    \t\t\treturn os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, strings.TrimPrefix(path, \"./\")))\r\n    \t\t}\r\n    \t\ta, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".forgejo/workflows/a.yml\"))\r\n    \t\tif err != nil {\r\n    \t\t\tpanic(err)\r\n    \t\t}\r\n    \t\twfs, err := jobparser.Parse(a, false, jobparser.ExpandLocalReusableWorkflows(fetch))\r\n    \t\tif err != nil {\r\n    \t\t\tpanic(err)\r\n    \t\t}\r\n    \t\tfmt.Printf(\"== %s\\n\", filepath.Base(root))\r\n    \t\tfor _, w := range wfs {\r\n    \t\t\tid, _ := w.Job()\r\n    \t\t\tkeys := []string{}\r\n    \t\t\tfor k, v := range w.Env {\r\n    \t\t\t\tkeys = append(keys, k+\"=\"+v)\r\n    \t\t\t}\r\n    \t\t\tsort.Strings(keys)\r\n    \t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"   job %-18s workflow-level env: %v\\n\", id, keys)\r\n    \t\t}\r\n    \t}\r\n    }"
      },
